  <RHAH_Follow_I-002>The mother who left them</RHAH_Follow_I-002>
  <RHAH_Follow_I-002_Text>The young ratkin left near the colony are still here. We do not know whether their mother is still alive. If she returned, would she recognize her children?</RHAH_Follow_I-002_Text>
  <RHAH_Follow_I-012>A child among the goods</RHAH_Follow_I-012>
  <RHAH_Follow_I-012_Text>The children bought from that caravan are still here. One trade was followed by meals, one after another.</RHAH_Follow_I-012_Text>
  <RHAH_Follow_I-013>The one traded away</RHAH_Follow_I-013>
  <RHAH_Follow_I-013_Text>The ratkin brought here to be traded is still here. If a child really had been traded away, where would they be now?</RHAH_Follow_I-013_Text>
  <RHAH_Follow_I-019>The child they asked for</RHAH_Follow_I-019>
  <RHAH_Follow_I-019_Text>The ratkin who once came asking for a baby is still here. If a child really had been handed over, how would the new caretakers have treated them? We do not know.</RHAH_Follow_I-019_Text>
  <RHAH_Follow_I-032>After the airdrop</RHAH_Follow_I-032>
  <RHAH_Follow_I-032_Text>The ratkin who arrived here are still here. Perhaps someone still has their pictures and names, and is still looking for them.</RHAH_Follow_I-032_Text>
  <RHAH_Follow_I-033>Begging</RHAH_Follow_I-033>
  <RHAH_Follow_I-033_Text>The ratkin who called someone Mommy is still here. It seems the child was simply making use of a kind heart to get a meal.</RHAH_Follow_I-033_Text>
  <RHAH_Follow_I-037>The mother who left sick</RHAH_Follow_I-037>
  <RHAH_Follow_I-037_Text>What became of the mother who left her young here? If she is still alive, she probably wants to know how they are doing.</RHAH_Follow_I-037_Text>
  <RHAH_Follow_I-041>The orphan who stayed</RHAH_Follow_I-041>
  <RHAH_Follow_I-041_Text>The ratkin orphan who arrived here is still here. Life has to go on, even without a mother beside them.</RHAH_Follow_I-041_Text>
